James sought guidance on sending a survey to the general public and inquired about potential costs. I outlined a step-by-step approach, recommending survey platforms like Google Forms for free options or SurveyMonkey for advanced features at a cost. I emphasized the importance of defining the target audience and preparing clear questions. Distribution methods included social media, email lists, and paid ads for broader outreach. I mentioned using panel services for specific demographics, which may incur fees. I clarified that costs will vary based on desired specificity and reach, advising that budgeting for paid distribution might be beneficial for large-scale, representative samples.
